Z||000000||goldfinger||11-17-1999||12:11 AM||||Ok im gonna buy a fiero dunno what year or anything but i have my sites on a couple around here anyhow the system i wanna get is:<BR>pioneer 4x10's <BR>compent speakers sony expod 6" 1/2 with the tweeter and crossover<BR>replace the 6" with the 6: 1/2 inch and surface mount the tweeters in the corners of the roof in the front then get an amp a fosgate punch 360a.. ok heres my plan mount that amp on the firewall of the fiero right behind the driver seat take 1"1/2 in PVC pipe put it to the back of the car where the 2 compartments are in the back and make it go up to the front next to each seat 2 pipes total to hear all the bass from the back and to run wires then put some 12" infinty kappas back there or some 10" kappas. A guy at soundpro my local car stereo place told me this would work well what do u all think?? or i was thinking get 4x6 to replace the factorys and then pop in some 3"1/2 beside them and it would all work out smooth but to top it all off get a sony mobile es deck for about 300$ and an pioneer eq for about 200$.. input on this system please i think it should sound great the lows are good the highs are good and the mids are good as well what do u all think?||||reg||12
Z||000001||RZURCTN||11-17-1999||11:07 AM||||Just keep in mind that there is an awful lot of heat in the engine compartment next to the firewall.  You may consider the the spare tire compartment or the "trunk" as a place to mount your amp.  I current use Panasonic 4x10's in the front and have great results.  How you set up your system is totally based on your own preferences.  If you like it, go for it!<BR>Ted||||reg||1
